label ch30_12:
    [   0] m "Hey, did you know I'm vegetarian?"
    [   1] m "Ah... I don't mean that like I'm bragging or anything!"
    [   2] m "I just thought you'd enjoy a fun fact about me."
    [   3] m "I decided to start a couple years ago after learning more about Earth's climate..."
    [   4] m "The carbon footprint of cultivating livestock is just unbelievable."
    [   5] m "Anyway, I decided it's not much of a personal sacrifice to just stop contributing to that whole mess."
    [   6] m "What, is that so strange of a reason?"
    [   7] m "Well, I guess a lot of people are more concerned about it being inhumane and all that..."
    [   8] m "I don't really care as much about that part."
    [   9] m "It's weird, like we only care about killing the things that we personally relate to as a species."
    [  10] m "Most people are fine with killing bugs because they're icky."
    [  11] m "And of course, we all kill billions of microorganisms daily without even giving it thought."
    [  12] m "But suddenly, if they're just a little bit bigger, it's murder!"
    [  13] m "I mean, what if plants feel some kind of pain too, and we just don't understand it?"
    [  14] m "What if pulling leaves off a stem feels like someone ripping off your fingers one by one?"
    [  15] m "I'm just saying, we're a pretty biased species, if you think about it."
    [  16] m "Anyway, if you ever feel like making a small contribution to the planet, it doesn't hurt to choose veggies once in a while!"
    [  17] m "Even if we ever have dinner together, and you just did it for me...that would be really romantic."
